  "stem": "Which equation is equivalent to \\(9x - 3y = 21\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(y = 3x - 7\\)",
    "B": "\\(y = -3x + 7\\)",
    "C": "\\(y = 3x + 7\\)",
    "D": "\\(y = 9x - 21\\)"
  },
  "answer": "A",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Subtract \\(9x\\): \\(-3y = -9x + 21\\).",
    "Divide by \\(-3\\): \\(y = 3x - 7\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Correct. \\(-3y = -9x + 21\\), and dividing by \\(-3\\) gives \\(y = 3x - 7\\).",
    "B": "Incorrect. Dividing \\(-9x + 21\\) by \\(-3\\) changes both signs: \\(3x - 7\\).",
    "C": "Incorrect. \\(21 \\div (-3) = -7\\), not \\(7\\).",
    "D": "Incorrect. Both sides must still be divided by \\(-3\\) after moving \\(9x\\)."
  },
